        <!--
          The agenda: fourteen days of the diary, full board only.

          ⚠️ This is the one region that is NOT wrap_content, and that is the point of it. Every
          other region is sized by what it says, so the board used to end ~590dp down however tall
          the widget was — and on the owner's phone that left the bottom two fifths of the widget
          empty. The list is `0dp` with a weight, so it takes every dp the other regions do not use,
          at any height, and scrolls for the rest. The heading row above it says how much there is.

          The list is filled with RemoteCollectionItems (API 31, this app's floor), so there is no
          RemoteViewsService and nothing to keep alive; its rows are `widget_agenda_day.xml` and
          `widget_agenda_event.xml`. When there is nothing to list — or the calendar may not be
          read — the list is hidden and `widget_board_agenda_empty` says which of those it is.
        -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/widget_board_agenda_head_row"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:orientation="horizontal"
            android:visibility="gone">

